WEBVTT

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:09.980
This is a work of fiction based on research into the period in which it is set. The people,
 organization, laws, and names that appear in it have no relation to any in the real world.

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:25.880
What was the "important mission"?

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:27.460
It's not a mission.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:31.840
I hear Ltg. Nakajima asked you
for something in person.

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:33.550
What was it?

00:00:35.390 --> 00:00:38.060
He asked me to take his daughter.

00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:39.350
What?

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:41.020
That's all.

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:42.860
"All"?

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:44.020
You moron!

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:47.070
Don't look so gloomy! That's great news!

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:48.860
Now, drink up!

00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:51.200
You're gonna tell me all about it!

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:56.370
This is great news!

00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:58.290
Yamagami, walk straight.

00:00:58.290 --> 00:01:00.290
Listen, everybody!

00:01:00.290 --> 00:01:04.040
This impregnable fortress
of a man, Yoshinobu Maeda,

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:08.380
is finally going to surrender and take a bride!

00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:10.420
Don't shout. It's disgraceful.

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:13.680
Misaki.

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:16.810
I've come to greet you.

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:54.020
Frailty, Thy Name Is...

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:00.490
It must have been hard.

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:01.950
I'm used to it.

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:06.250
I learned something new about you.
That makes me happy.

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:11.300
I want to know more about you.

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:13.510
We have plenty of time.

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:25.350
Check.

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:34.280
What's wrong? That's not like you.

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:36.530
Nothing.

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:39.910
Father, someone is here for you.

00:03:39.910 --> 00:03:42.740
I'm here to escort you, sir.

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:44.620
Oh, Colonel Maeda.

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:47.210
Are you all playing shogi together?

00:03:47.210 --> 00:03:51.420
You talk too much, Moriyama.

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:53.380
I'm sorry.

00:03:53.380 --> 00:03:55.510
Oh, sir, we need to hurry.

00:03:55.510 --> 00:03:58.510
Oh, you're right.

00:03:58.510 --> 00:03:59.890
I'll accompany you.

00:03:59.890 --> 00:04:05.020
I'm just going to listen to Okimura
grumble. I'll be fine on my own.

00:04:05.020 --> 00:04:08.310
You should take your time relaxing.

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:11.440
Misaki will be happier that way.

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:22.410
How good to see the moon!

00:04:23.490 --> 00:04:27.080
She is like a little piece of money,

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:30.710
a little silver flower.

00:04:30.710 --> 00:04:33.920
She is cold and chaste.

00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:38.300
I am sure she is a virgin.

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:41.340
Who was that who cried out?

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:45.510
Ah, the prophet! He of whom
the Tetrarch is afraid?

00:04:45.510 --> 00:04:47.430
It is thy mouth...

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:52.900
To kiss thy mouth, my lips to thy lips,
my words to thy words.

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:57.780
It is thy mouth that I desire, Jokanaan.

00:05:27.510 --> 00:05:30.310
Next is here and here!

00:05:30.310 --> 00:05:34.650
I see. Their movements
are becoming disorganized.

00:05:34.650 --> 00:05:35.610
Ah.

00:05:35.610 --> 00:05:37.270
Is something wrong?

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:38.940
Here.

00:05:37.350 --> 00:05:41.610
Tokyo Station

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:40.820
Big, aren't they?

00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:42.360
Yeah.

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:45.070
Kurusu is holding out.

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:47.870
A lot of little ones are moving, too!

00:05:47.870 --> 00:05:51.710
Are the vampire units being drawn in as well?

00:05:51.710 --> 00:05:56.170
It's like... they're gathering
to Colonel Maeda out of longing.

00:05:56.170 --> 00:05:57.340
Why?

00:05:57.340 --> 00:06:00.380
Maybe they're dreaming.

00:06:00.380 --> 00:06:03.470
There are things even I don't understand.

00:06:03.470 --> 00:06:05.470
There are?

00:06:05.470 --> 00:06:07.430
Hmm?

00:06:07.430 --> 00:06:09.720
You sure are amazing.

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:12.850
You know right where the vampire units are.

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:14.230
Amazing?

00:06:14.230 --> 00:06:16.520
He said that we're amazing.

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:17.520
Yeah.

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:19.980
Keep going a little longer.

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:25.030
If we make it to morning without anyone
who's "it" finding us, we win.

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:41.300
I shall clear a path for you.

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:42.710
Thank you!

00:06:47.470 --> 00:06:48.890
Shutaro!

00:07:07.490 --> 00:07:09.030
Mr. Maeda.

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:16.870
Vampires, there are two roads open to you!

00:07:16.870 --> 00:07:18.130
One!

00:07:18.130 --> 00:07:23.130
Obey us, Special Forces Unit 16,
and you will receive blood and registrations!

00:07:23.130 --> 00:07:24.130
Two!

00:07:24.130 --> 00:07:26.180
Refuse to obey, and...

00:07:35.850 --> 00:07:38.810
Mr. Maeda, no matter what...

00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:41.940
Mr. Maeda!

00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:55.790
You don't recognize me, do you?

00:07:58.460 --> 00:08:01.040
We're getting two new members?

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:05.090
One is my classmate.
He's been stationed in England.

00:08:05.090 --> 00:08:07.380
Oh, Yamagami.

00:08:07.380 --> 00:08:10.340
He's really lucky he got to become a vampire.

00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:12.640
But he's unranked.

00:08:12.640 --> 00:08:14.010
That idiot.

00:08:14.010 --> 00:08:15.600
Useless, then.

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:17.770
Even blunt tools have uses.

00:08:17.770 --> 00:08:18.980
And the other?

00:08:18.980 --> 00:08:22.400
Shutaro Kurusu, an A-class vampire.

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:24.070
That's wonderful!

00:08:24.070 --> 00:08:25.690
A-class, huh?

00:08:25.690 --> 00:08:28.740
You don't see many of those in this country.

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:31.740
That one's a sharp tool, then.

00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:34.660
That depends on how he's trained.

00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:35.990
Oh?

00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:38.500
You look happy, Maeda.

00:08:38.500 --> 00:08:39.500
Me?

00:08:39.500 --> 00:08:41.080
Yes.

00:08:41.080 --> 00:08:43.210
What nonsense.

00:08:52.010 --> 00:08:53.470
Mr. Maeda!

00:08:54.560 --> 00:08:56.430
Vampire...

00:09:00.770 --> 00:09:05.020
There are so many more things
I wanted to learn from you!

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:27.550
So, I'm the only survivor.

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:34.600
Once the sun sets, I'll look at the sky.

00:09:34.600 --> 00:09:37.640
The Big Dipper never moves.

00:09:41.440 --> 00:09:45.560
I don't know any way to live except by fighting.

00:09:56.080 --> 00:09:57.530
Yoshinobu Maeda!

00:09:57.530 --> 00:09:59.950
You saved my life, Colonel Nakajima!

00:09:59.950 --> 00:10:02.500
Please use it however you see fit!

00:10:02.500 --> 00:10:06.170
I'm only glad that you're safe.

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:11.510
I won't leave you alone again.

00:10:24.650 --> 00:10:26.810
Are you awake now?

00:10:28.770 --> 00:10:30.150
Yeah.

00:10:31.570 --> 00:10:33.490
What's wrong?

00:10:33.490 --> 00:10:35.610
Your sleep was troubled.

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:41.790
I was having a strange dream.

00:10:41.790 --> 00:10:44.870
I dreamed I was visiting graves.

00:10:44.870 --> 00:10:47.000
There was one for Moriyama.

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:49.210
He was with Code Zero, wasn't he?

00:10:49.210 --> 00:10:50.880
Yeah.

00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:53.970
Yamagami's grave is there, too.

00:10:53.970 --> 00:10:56.340
And so is yours.

00:10:58.470 --> 00:11:01.560
I'm all alone.

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:06.560
What a strange dream.

00:11:11.980 --> 00:11:13.070
Hey,

00:11:13.070 --> 00:11:16.030
where should I go?

00:11:17.610 --> 00:11:20.450
Take me with you.

00:11:20.450 --> 00:11:22.160
Shutaro!

00:11:24.200 --> 00:11:26.000
Misaki...

00:11:29.130 --> 00:11:30.750
Why did you come here?!

00:11:30.750 --> 00:11:33.050
Because you left without telling me!

00:11:33.050 --> 00:11:34.470
Stay away!

00:11:39.640 --> 00:11:42.890
Find someplace in the sun, Aoi.

00:11:42.890 --> 00:11:46.190
We can't follow you there.

00:11:46.190 --> 00:11:47.690
Shutaro.

00:11:51.110 --> 00:11:52.780
I am...

00:11:53.820 --> 00:11:57.950
Mr. Maeda, please come back to us.

00:11:57.950 --> 00:11:59.910
I-I am...

00:11:59.910 --> 00:12:01.160
Mr. Maeda!

00:12:07.710 --> 00:12:09.830
Kurusu...

00:12:23.140 --> 00:12:25.720
Kurusu...

00:12:27.560 --> 00:12:29.060
Mr. Maeda.

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:33.320
Kurusu.

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:39.150
That softness will get your friends killed.

00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:46.370
I am soft.

00:12:46.370 --> 00:12:50.080
But what's so wrong about that?

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:51.750
I'm soft.

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:55.090
Isn't that what makes me human?

00:12:55.090 --> 00:12:56.380
Mr. Maeda?!

00:13:13.860 --> 00:13:16.650
Children of the future age,

00:13:16.650 --> 00:13:21.450
Reading this indignant page,

00:13:21.450 --> 00:13:24.870
Know that in a former time

00:13:24.870 --> 00:13:30.330
Love, sweet love, was thought a crime.

00:13:30.330 --> 00:13:32.790
In the age of gold,

00:13:32.790 --> 00:13:36.340
Free from winter's cold,

00:13:36.340 --> 00:13:41.180
Youth and maiden bright,
To the holy light,

00:13:41.180 --> 00:13:46.260
Naked in the sunny beams delight.

00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:50.270
Once a youthful pair,

00:13:50.270 --> 00:13:54.940
Filled with softest care,

00:13:54.940 --> 00:13:57.520
Met in garden bright

00:13:57.520 --> 00:14:01.110
Where the holy light

00:14:01.110 --> 00:14:06.080
Had just removed the curtains of the night.

00:14:07.870 --> 00:14:10.330
Then, in rising day,

00:14:10.330 --> 00:14:14.290
On the grass they play;

00:14:14.290 --> 00:14:16.540
Parents were afar,

00:14:16.540 --> 00:14:19.630
Strangers came not near,

00:14:19.630 --> 00:14:23.880
And the maiden soon forgot her fear.

00:14:23.880 --> 00:14:27.930
Tired with kisses sweet,

00:14:27.930 --> 00:14:31.180
They agree to meet

00:14:31.180 --> 00:14:33.310
When the silent sleep

00:14:33.310 --> 00:14:36.610
Waves o'er heaven's deep...

00:15:50.010 --> 00:15:51.600
Kurusu.

00:15:51.600 --> 00:15:53.020
Mr. Maeda?

00:15:57.140 --> 00:15:59.810
You're still soft.

00:15:59.810 --> 00:16:00.980
Huh?

00:16:03.190 --> 00:16:04.320
Mr. Maeda!

00:16:04.320 --> 00:16:06.400
Lance Corporal Kurusu!

00:16:06.400 --> 00:16:08.240
Y-Yes, sir!

00:16:08.240 --> 00:16:12.950
Put an end to this ridiculous farce.

00:16:14.580 --> 00:16:16.370
Please.

00:16:16.370 --> 00:16:18.000
Mr. Maeda...

00:16:32.300 --> 00:16:35.850
I guess I wasn't alone after all.

00:16:38.890 --> 00:16:42.020
Colonel Yoshinobu Maeda

00:16:42.020 --> 00:16:45.530
hereby concludes his mission.

00:17:09.260 --> 00:17:10.880
Shutaro.

00:17:14.430 --> 00:17:17.270
Is it over?

00:17:17.270 --> 00:17:19.230
Yes.

00:17:19.230 --> 00:17:22.650
You won't have to fight anymore?

00:17:35.580 --> 00:17:37.330
I have to go.

00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:40.290
You're bleeding!

00:17:40.290 --> 00:17:44.920
If I weren't a vampire, I'd be dead.

00:17:44.920 --> 00:17:46.460
Idiot.

00:17:50.800 --> 00:17:52.550
Aoi.

00:17:52.550 --> 00:17:53.640
What?

00:17:53.640 --> 00:17:56.350
Would you give me your blood?

00:17:56.350 --> 00:17:57.310
Huh?

00:17:57.310 --> 00:18:00.560
I want you to make me a vampire.

00:18:05.270 --> 00:18:06.940
Please.

00:18:10.150 --> 00:18:12.740
Stay human...

00:18:12.740 --> 00:18:14.950
Aoi?

00:18:14.950 --> 00:18:18.450
Stay human, Shutaro!

00:18:20.620 --> 00:18:23.120
That's why, Aoi.

00:18:25.250 --> 00:18:26.880
Shutaro?

00:18:26.880 --> 00:18:30.630
Whether I'm a human or a vampire,

00:18:30.630 --> 00:18:33.510
I fight because I want to keep my humanity.

00:19:24.850 --> 00:19:26.310
Shutaro!

00:19:35.320 --> 00:19:36.280
Oh.

00:19:36.280 --> 00:19:38.200
Wow.

00:19:38.200 --> 00:19:40.200
Kurusu.

00:19:40.200 --> 00:19:41.120
Kurusu.

00:19:41.120 --> 00:19:42.580
What is this?

00:19:50.920 --> 00:19:53.710
Who... are you?

00:19:57.510 --> 00:19:59.760
I'm Shutaro Kurusu.

00:20:19.910 --> 00:20:24.750
Will you always keep walking, Shutaro?

00:20:24.750 --> 00:20:28.460
For ten, 20, 30 years?

00:20:28.460 --> 00:20:32.290
I'll end up turning into an old lady.

00:20:34.050 --> 00:20:38.010
The brief instant when the curtain falls.

00:20:43.390 --> 00:20:46.850
The gap between reality and fiction.

00:20:48.390 --> 00:20:49.940
That

00:20:49.940 --> 00:20:52.110
is where we live.

00:20:53.650 --> 00:20:56.820
Frailty, thy name is...

00:20:56.820 --> 00:20:58.610
...vampire.

00:21:00.410 --> 00:21:04.410
Vampires, there are two roads open to you!

00:21:04.410 --> 00:21:05.620
One!

00:21:05.620 --> 00:21:11.580
Obey us, Special Forces Unit 16,
and you will receive blood and registrations!

00:21:11.580 --> 00:21:12.540
Two!

00:21:12.540 --> 00:21:17.590
Refuse to obey, and we will end
your bloodlines here and now!

00:23:25.260 --> 00:23:29.350
All the world’s a stage,
And all the men and women merely players;

00:23:29.350 --> 00:23:32.430
They have their exits and their entrances;

00:23:32.430 --> 00:23:37.940
And one man in his time plays many parts.

00:23:37.940 --> 00:23:40.020
But...

00:23:40.020 --> 00:23:42.820
...we are outside all that.
